    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen a file is reloaded from disk, either by `autoread` or manually using `:edit`, it's hard to see what actually changed in the buffer.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nA \"diff\" showing the changes should be displayed in the buffer.\n\n### Investigation\n\nI have a [plugin](https://github.com/micampe/autoread-diff.nvim) implementing something like this; when discussing it on irc it was suggested I file it as a feature request.\n\nThe implementation revealed a couple of limitations for a good solution:\n- #40457 I could not find a reliable reactive way to get the content of the buffer *before* the reload happens\n- #40456 `vim.text.diff` only returns line diffs, I believe the `inline` variants are essential for this use case",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
